 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Singularity at $u_2=0$:** If a particle is at the center of projection, the Jacobian is undefined. Guard against division by zero or clamp $u_2$ to a minimum value [S6, unofficial].
-*   **Precision:** The determinant calculations and matrix inversions can suffer from precision issues if the splat is extremely elongated or small. Use stable linear algebra routines [S13].
-*   **Overlap Assumption:** The back-to-front compositing formula assumes kernels do not overlap along the ray. If they do, the attenuation term $\prod (1 - g_j q_j)$ becomes inaccurate, potentially causing visual artifacts [S8, unofficial].
