 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N \cdot A)$, where $N$ is the number of particles and $A$ is the average number of pixels covered by a splat. The computation of the EWA filter (matrix inversion, determinant) is done per particle, making it more expensive per particle than simple splatting, but the rasterization is efficient.
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ to store particle data and splat primitives. The image buffer is $O(W \cdot H)$.
